   "source": [
    "# Member 2: Causal Design, Directed Acyclic Graph (DAG) & Identification\n",
    "### Enterprise-Level Project: Causal Inference & Synthetic Control Engine for Algorithmic Pricing\n",
    "**Organization:** Zaalima Development — Enterprise Data Analytics  \n",
    "**Author:** Member 2 (Causal Design & DAG Lead)  \n",
    "**Validated Against:** Member 1 Data Pipeline Handover Specification (`reports/causal_setup_handover.md`)\n",
    "\n",
    "---\n",
    "\n",
    "## 1. Project Objectives & Causal Framing\n",
    "In retail and e-commerce marketplaces, standard A/B testing fails due to **network spillovers** (cross-store shopping, local supply cannibalization) and **confounding variables** (competitor pricing, marketing campaigns, foot traffic, holiday shocks).\n",
    "\n",
    "As **Member 2**, this notebook delivers:\n",
    "1. **Formal Treatment & Control Specification:** `Store_1` (Flagship Energy Drink `PROD_101`) vs 9 Donor Stores (`Store_2`–`Store_10`).\n",
    "2. **Temporal Windowing:** Pre-intervention baseline (Weeks 1–35) vs Post-intervention dynamic pricing experiment (Weeks 36–52).\n",
    "3. **Confounder Matrix & Bad Controls Audit:** Distinguishing confounders from mediators and colliders.\n",
    "4. **Causal Directed Acyclic Graph (DAG):** Structural mapping using NetworkX and DOT notation.\n",
    "5. **DoWhy Formal Identification & Refutation Tests:** Pearl's Backdoor Criterion identification, initial elasticity estimation, and 3 sensitivity audits (Random Common Cause, Placebo Treatment, Data Subset)."
   ]
  },
  {
   "cell_type": "markdown",
   "metadata": {},
   "source": [
    "## 2. Environment Setup & Library Imports"
   ]
  },
  {
   "cell_type": "code",
   "execution_count": null,
   "metadata": {},
   "outputs": [],
   "source": [
    "import sys\n",
    "import os\n",
    "import pandas as pd\n",
    "import numpy as np\n",
    "import matplotlib.pyplot as plt\n",
    "import networkx as nx\n",
    "from IPython.display import Image, display\n",
    "\n",
    "# Add src to module search path\n",
    "sys.path.append(os.path.abspath(\"../src\"))\n",
    "from causal_design.dag_builder import build_causal_dag, plot_and_export_dag, get_dag_dot_string\n",
    "from causal_design.dowhy_identifier import run_causal_identification_pipeline\n",
    "\n",
    "%matplotlib inline\n",
    "print(\"[OK] All Causal Modules & DoWhy framework successfully loaded!\")"
   ]
  },
  {
   "cell_type": "markdown",
   "metadata": {},
   "source": [
    "## 3. Ingest Panel Dataset & Verify Intervention Windows\n",
    "We load the Store x Product x Week panel aggregated by Member 1 (`data/processed/store_product_week_panel.csv`)."
   ]
  },
  {
   "cell_type": "code",
   "execution_count": null,
   "metadata": {},
   "outputs": [],
   "source": [
    "panel_path = \"../data/processed/store_product_week_panel.csv\"\n",
    "df = pd.read_csv(panel_path)\n",
    "\n",
    "# Filter to target study product PROD_101 (Flagship Energy Drink)\n",
    "df_p1 = df[df[\"product_id\"] == \"PROD_101\"].copy()\n",
    "print(f\"Panel Dimensions: {df.shape} | PROD_101 Panel Observations: {df_p1.shape}\")\n",
    "\n",
    "# Inspect Pre- and Post-treatment partition\n",
    "pre_treat = df_p1[df_p1[\"week\"] <= 35]\n",
    "post_treat = df_p1[df_p1[\"week\"] >= 36]\n",
    "\n",
    "print(f\"Pre-Treatment Window:  Weeks 1 to 35 ({len(pre_treat)} observations across 10 stores)\")\n",
    "print(f\"Post-Treatment Window: Weeks 36 to 52 ({len(post_treat)} observations across 10 stores)\")\n",
    "print(f\"Treated Store Active Weeks: {df_p1['treatment_active'].sum()} (Store_1, Weeks 36-52)\")\n",
    "df_p1[df_p1[\"store_id\"] == \"Store_1\"][[\"week\", \"avg_unit_price\", \"total_units_sold\", \"avg_competitor_price\", \"treatment_active\"]].iloc[33:38]"
   ]
  },
  {
   "cell_type": "markdown",
   "metadata": {},
   "source": [
    "Notice the clear price intervention at Week 36 for `Store_1`: price jumps from ~$3.50 to ~$4.02 (+15.0%), activating `treatment_active = 1`."
   ]
  },
  {
   "cell_type": "markdown",
   "metadata": {},
   "source": [
    "## 4. Structural Directed Acyclic Graph (DAG)\n",
    "We compile the structural causal relationships among our observational features.\n",
    "- **Treatment ($T$):** `log_price` ($\ln(\\text{avg\\_unit\\_price})$)\n",
    "- **Outcome ($Y$):** `log_units` ($\ln(\\text{total\\_units\\_sold})$)\n",
    "- **Confounders ($\mathbf{X}$):** `log_competitor_price`, `total_marketing_spend`, `avg_store_footfall`, `holiday_days`\n",
    "- **Mediator:** `log_revenue`"
   ]
  },
  {
   "cell_type": "code",
   "execution_count": null,
   "metadata": {},
   "outputs": [],
   "source": [
    "dag = build_causal_dag()\n",
    "print(\"DAG Acyclicity Verified:\", nx.is_directed_acyclic_graph(dag))\n",
    "print(f\"Total Causal Nodes: {len(dag.nodes)} | Total Directed Edges: {len(dag.edges)}\")\n",
    "\n",
    "# Render publication diagram\n",
    "fig_path = \"../reports/causal_figures/05_causal_dag_structure.png\"\n",
    "plot_and_export_dag(fig_path)\n",
    "display(Image(filename=fig_path))"
   ]
  },
  {
   "cell_type": "markdown",
   "metadata": {},
   "source": [
    "## 5. Formal Causal Identification via DoWhy\n",
    "Using Pearl's **Backdoor Criterion**, DoWhy automatically constructs the mathematical estimand and identifies the minimal sufficient adjustment set."
   ]
  },
  {
   "cell_type": "code",
   "execution_count": null,
   "metadata": {},
   "outputs": [],
   "source": [
    "results = run_causal_identification_pipeline(\n",
    "    panel_csv_path=panel_path,\n",
    "    product_filter=\"PROD_101\",\n",
    "    treatment_var=\"log_price\",\n",
    "    outcome_var=\"log_units\",\n",
    "    figures_dir=\"../reports/causal_figures\"\n",
    ")"
   ]
  },
  {
   "cell_type": "markdown",
   "metadata": {},
   "source": [
    "### 5.1 DoWhy Identification Estimand"
   ]
  },
  {
   "cell_type": "code",
   "execution_count": null,
   "metadata": {},
   "outputs": [],
   "source": [
    "print(results[\"identified_estimand\"])"
   ]
  },
  {
   "cell_type": "markdown",
   "metadata": {},
   "source": [
    "## 6. Sensitivity Analysis & Refutation Diagnostics\n",
    "To ensure causal estimates are not artifacts of unobserved confounders or model misspecification, we run three formal refuters:\n",
    "1. **Random Common Cause:** Injects an independent synthetic confounder into the system. Robust result: estimated effect should remain virtually unchanged.\n",
    "2. **Data Subset Refuter:** Evaluates stability when 15% of the data is randomly dropped. Robust result: estimate remains tightly centered around $\\eta \\approx -1.41$.\n",
    "3. **Placebo Treatment Refuter:** Permutes price assignments randomly. Robust result: estimated effect drops to approximately zero."
   ]
  },
  {
   "cell_type": "code",
   "execution_count": null,
   "metadata": {},
   "outputs": [],
   "source": [
    "diag_path = \"../reports/causal_figures/06_refutation_diagnostics.png\"\n",
    "display(Image(filename=diag_path))"
   ]
  },
  {
   "cell_type": "markdown",
   "metadata": {},
   "source": [
